== 2. The Great: Against the Saints

#strong[The second device that Satan has to ensnare and destroy the great and honorable of the earth is,]

BY engaging them against the people of the Most High, against those who are his jewels, his pleasant portion, the delight of his eye and the joy of his heart, etc. So he drew Pharaoh to engage#footnote[Exod 14.] against the children of Israel, and that was his overthrow. So he engaged#footnote[Esth 7.] Haman against the Jews, and so brought him to hang on the gallows that he had made for Mordecai. So he engaged#footnote[Dan 6.] those princes and administrators against Daniel, which was the utter ruin of them and their families. So in Revelation 20:7, 8, 9:#footnote[Rev 20:7, 8, 9.] “When the thousand years are complete, Satan will be released from his prison, and will go out to deceive the nations in the four corners of the earth—Gog and Magog—to assemble them for battle. Their number is like the sand of the seashore. And they marched across the broad expanse of the earth and surrounded the camp of the saints and the beloved city. But fire came down from heaven and consumed them.”

#strong[Now the remedies against this device of Satan are as follows.]

The first #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that none have engaged against the#footnote[As was once said of the Greeks in the epigram, whom their enemies thought invulnerable: “We shoot at them, but they do not fall down; we wound them, and do not kill them,” etc.] saints without being ruined by the God of the saints. Divine justice has been too hard for all who have opposed and engaged against the saints, as is evident in Saul, Pharaoh, Haman, etc. “He rebuked kings on their behalf: ‘Do not touch My anointed ones! Do no harm to My prophets!’” When men of Balaam’s spirit and principles have engaged against the saints, how the angel of the Lord has met them in the way and jostled their bones against the wall! How he has broken their backs and necks, and by his drawn sword cut them off in the prime of their days and in the height of their sins! Ah! What a harvest hell has had#footnote[#emph[Tanto plus gloriae referemus quanto plures superabimus:] the number of opposers makes the Christians’ conquest the more illustrious, said Paedarelus in Erasmus.] in our days of those who have engaged against the Lamb, and against those who are called, chosen and faithful! Ah, how divine justice has poured out their blood like water on the ground! How God has laid their honor and glory in the dust! In the pride and madness of their hearts they said, as Pharaoh did, “We will pursue, we will overtake, we will divide the spoil; our lusts will be satisfied on them; we will draw our sword, our hand will destroy them.” #emph[In the things in which they have spoken and acted proudly, justice has been above them.] History abounds in nothing more than in examples of this kind, etc.

The second #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to dwell for some time every morning on the following Scriptures, in which God has engaged himself to stand by his people and for his people, and to make them victorious over the greatest and wisest of their enemies.#footnote[Isa 8:9, 10.] “Huddle together” (says the Lord by the prophet) “O peoples,#footnote[#emph[Occidi poterant sed vinci non poterant] \[They could be killed, but they could not be conquered\], said Cyprian of the Christians in his time.] and be shattered; pay attention, all you#super[+] distant lands; prepare for battle, and be shattered; prepare for battle, and be shattered! Devise a plan, but it will be thwarted; state a proposal, but it will not happen. For God is with us.” “Do not fear, O worm of Jacob,”#footnote[Isa 41:14, 15.] “O few men of Israel. I will help you,” declares the #smallcaps[Lord]. “Your Redeemer is the Holy One of Israel. Behold, I will make you into a threshing sledge, new and sharp, with many teeth. You will thresh the mountains and crush them, and reduce the hills to chaff.”#footnote[Verse 16.] “You will winnow them, and a wind will carry them away; a gale will scatter them. But you will rejoice in the #smallcaps[Lord]; you will glory in the Holy One of Israel.” “No weapon formed against#footnote[Isa 54:17.] you shall prosper, and you will refute every tongue that accuses you. This is the heritage of the servants of the #smallcaps[Lord], and their vindication is from Me,” declares the #smallcaps[Lord]. “But now many#footnote[Mic 4:11.] nations have assembled against you, saying, ‘Let her be defiled, and let us feast our eyes on Zion.’ But they do not know#footnote[Verse 12.] the thoughts of the #smallcaps[Lord] or understand His plan, for He has gathered them like sheaves to the threshing floor. Rise and thresh,#footnote[Verse 13.] O Daughter of Zion, for I will give you horns of iron and hooves of bronze to break to pieces many peoples. Then you will devote their gain to the #smallcaps[Lord], their wealth to the Lord of all the earth.”#footnote[Zech 12:2, 3.] “Behold, I will make Jerusalem a cup of drunkenness to all the surrounding peoples. Judah will be besieged, as well as Jerusalem. On that day, when all the nations of the earth gather against her, I will make Jerusalem a heavy stone for all the peoples; all who would heave it away will be severely injured.”

The third #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider that if you#super[+] engage against the saints, you must#footnote[Acts 5:39. It seems to be drawn from the fable of the Giants, who were said to make war with the gods.] engage against God himself, because of that near and blessed union that is between God and them. You#super[+] cannot be fighters against the saints without being found, when the account is cast up, to be fighters against God himself. And what greater madness is there than for weakness itself to engage against almighty strength? The near union that is between the Lord and believers is set forth by the near union that is between a husband and his wife.#footnote[The soul’s happiness consists in nothing but its union with God, and its misery lies in nothing so much as in its disunion from God.] (“The two will become one flesh. This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church.”) “We are members of His body, of His flesh and of His bones,” says the apostle. This near union is set forth by the union that is between the head and the members, which make up one body, and by the union that is between the graft and the stock, which are made one by incision. The union between the Lord and a believer is so near that you#super[+] cannot strike a believer without the Lord feeling it and taking it as done to himself: “Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”#footnote[Acts 9:4. Isa 63:9.] “In all their distress, He too was afflicted,” etc. Ah souls! Who ever engaged against God and prospered? Who ever took up the sword against him and did not perish by it? God can speak you#super[+] to hell, and nod you to hell, at his pleasure. It is your#super[+] greatest concern to lay down your weapons at his feet, and to#footnote[Ps 2:12.] “kiss the Son, lest He be angry and you perish in your rebellion.”

The fourth #emph[remedy] against this #emph[device] of Satan is solemnly to consider that#footnote[#emph[Hic homo potuit apud Deum quod voluit,] said one concerning Luther: he could have from God whatever he wished.] you#super[+] are much indebted to the saints (as instruments) for the mercies that you enjoy, and for the preventing and removing of many a judgment that otherwise might have been your ruin before this day. Were it not for the saints’ sake, God would quickly make the heavens like brass and the earth like iron; God would quickly strip you of your robes and glory, and set you on the dunghill with Job. They are the props that keep the world from falling about your ears, and that keep the iron rod from breaking your bones. “So He said He would#footnote[Ps 106:23.] destroy them—had not Moses His chosen one stood before Him in the breach to divert#footnote[Prayer is (#emph[porta coeli, clavis Paradisi]) the gate of heaven, a key to let us into paradise.] His wrath from destroying them.”

Ah! Had not the saints many a time cast themselves into the breach between God’s wrath and you#super[+], you would have been cut off from the land of the living and had your portion with those whose names are written in the dust.#footnote[“When the danger is over, the saint is forgotten,” is a French proverb, and one that many saints in England have found true by experience.] Many a nation, many a city and many a family is surrounded with blessings for the sake of the Josephs who live in it, and is preserved from many calamities and miseries for the sake of the Moseses, the Daniels, the Noahs and the Jobs who dwell among them. That is a sweet word, Prov 10:25: “When the whirlwind passes, the wicked are no more, but the#footnote[יסוד עולם #emph[Jesodh gnolam] from #emph[Josadh.]] righteous are an everlasting foundation,” or, “are the foundation of the world.” The righteous are the foundation of the world, which but for their sakes would soon shatter and fall to ruin. So the psalmist, Ps 75:3: “When the earth and all its dwellers quake, it is I who bear up its pillars. Selah.”#footnote[Mary Queen of Scots, the mother of King James, used to say that she feared Mr. Knox’s prayer more than an army of ten thousand men.]

When the emperor Marcus Antoninus was in Germany with his army, he was shut in by his enemies in a dry country. They so stopped all the passages that he and his army were likely to perish for lack of water. The emperor’s lieutenant, seeing him so distressed, told him that he had heard that the Christians could obtain anything from their God by their prayers. So the emperor, having a legion of Christians in his army, asked them to pray to their God for his and the army’s deliverance out of that danger. They did so at once, and at once great thunder fell among the enemies, and abundant water on the Romans, so that their thirst was quenched and the enemies were overthrown without any fight. I shall close this last remedy with those sweet words of the psalmist: “God is known in Judah; His name is great#footnote[Ps 76:1, 2, 3.] in Israel. His tent is in Salem, His dwelling place in Zion. There He shattered the flaming arrows, the shield and sword and weapons of war. Selah.”
